# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# **The legacy security.txt location.** RFC 9116 puts the file at /.well-known/security.txt, and
# that is where it lives. Some researcher tooling still tries the document root first, and until
# 404.html shipped that path returned the homepage with a 200: an HTML page where a scanner
# expected a text file, which reads as "this project has no security contact". Sending them to the
# real file costs one line.
/security.txt  /.well-known/security.txt  301

# **www is redirected at the edge, not here.** A Cloudflare Redirect Rule handles it, because a
# _redirects file only runs once a request has already been routed to this project, and the point
# is for www never to serve a second copy of the site. Recorded here so the absence looks
# deliberate rather than forgotten. See site/README.md.
